Hard output rules:
- The response must start with { and end with }.
- Use double quotes for every JSON key and string value.
- Escape newlines inside JSON strings as \n.
- Do not include markdown fences.
- Do not include explanations.
- Do not include comments.
- Do not include text before or after the JSON.
{% else %}
Structured response schema:
- Return exactly one object with these fields:
  - imports: Python import lines as a string.
  - decorators: only icontract decorator lines as a string.
  - coverage: list of coverage items.
- Each coverage item must have exactly these fields:
  - contract_id: exact NLContract ID.
  - lowered_to: one of "require", "ensure", or "omitted".
  - expression: decorator string when lowered, otherwise "".
  - reason: short reason.
{% endif %}

Coverage requirements:
- Include exactly one coverage item for each NLContract ID.
- Use lowered_to="require" for preconditions lowered to @icontract.require.
- Use lowered_to="ensure" for postconditions lowered to @icontract.ensure.
- Use lowered_to="omitted" for resource bounds, ambiguous rules, unsupported rules, or too-expensive checks.

